{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing LL = int64_t;\nconstexpr int MOD = 1E9 + 7;\nint power(int a, int b) {\n    int ans = 1;\n    while (b > 0) {\n        if (b & 1)\n            ans = LL(ans) * a % MOD;\n        a = LL(a) * a % MOD;\n        b >>= 1;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<vector<int>> p(n);\n    for (auto &i : p) {\n        i.resize(n);\n        for (int &j : i) {\n            cin >> j;\n            j = LL(j) * power(100, MOD - 2) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    vector<vector<int>> id(n + 1);\n    vector<vector<int>> subsets(n + 1);\n    for (int sz = 0; sz <= n; ++sz) {\n        id[sz].resize(1 << n);\n        for (int s = 0; s < (1 << n); ++s)\n            if (__builtin_popcount(s) == sz) {\n                id[sz][s] = subsets[sz].size();\n                subsets[sz].push_back(s);\n            }\n    }\n    vector<map<LL, int>> families(n + 1);\n    families[0][1] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int s = 0; s < (1 << n); ++s) {\n            int pr = 1;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n                if (s >> j & 1)\n                    pr = LL(pr) * p[i - 1][j] % MOD;\n                else\n                    pr = LL(pr) * (1 + MOD - p[i - 1][j]) % MOD;\n            for (auto [f, _p] : families[i - 1]) {\n                LL mask = 0;\n                for (int t : subsets[i])\n                    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n                        if ((t >> j & 1) && (s >> j & 1) && (f >> id[i - 1][t ^ 1 << j] & 1)) {\n                            mask |= 1LL << id[i][t];\n                            break;\n                        }\n                families[i][mask] = (families[i][mask] + LL(_p) * pr) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << families[n][1] << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef power(a, b):\n    ans = 1\n    a %= MOD\n    while b > 0:\n        if b & 1:\n            ans = (ans * a) % MOD\n        a = (a * a) % MOD\n        b >>= 1\n    return ans\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    index = 1\n    \n    p = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        row = list(map(int, data[index:index+n]))\n        index += n\n        p.append(row)\n    \n    # Precompute modular inverse of 100\n    inv_100 = power(100, MOD - 2)\n    \n    # Normalize probabilities\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            p[i][j] = (p[i][j] * inv_100) % MOD\n    \n    # Precompute subsets and id mappings\n    id_map = {}\n    subsets = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    for sz in range(n + 1):\n        for s in range(1 << n):\n            if bin(s).count('1') == sz:\n                id_map[(sz, s)] = len(subsets[sz])\n                subsets[sz].append(s)\n    \n    # families[i] is a dictionary mapping mask -> probability\n    families = [defaultdict(int) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    families[0][1] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for s in range(1 << n):\n            # Compute probability for current state s\n            pr = 1\n            for j in range(n):\n                if (s >> j) & 1:\n                    pr = (pr * p[i-1][j]) % MOD\n                else:\n                    pr = (pr * (1 + MOD - p[i-1][j])) % MOD\n            \n            # Process all masks from previous family\n            for mask, prob in families[i-1].items():\n                new_mask = 0\n                # For each subset t of size i\n                for t in subsets[i]:\n                    # Check if condition holds for any j\n                    for j in range(n):\n                        if (t >> j) & 1 and (s >> j) & 1:\n                            # Check if in mask, the bit corresponding to t ^ (1 << j) in family i-1 is set\n                            prev_subset = t ^ (1 << j)\n                            if prev_subset in id_map and id_map[(i-1, prev_subset)] < 32:  # safety check\n                                prev_id = id_map[(i-1, prev_subset)]\n                                if (mask >> prev_id) & 1:\n                                    new_mask |= (1 << id_map[(i, t)])\n                                    break\n                \n                families[i][new_mask] = (families[i][new_mask] + prob * pr) % MOD\n    \n    print(families[n][1] % MOD)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001618731184862554, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.11761528253555298, -0.0002851079625543207, -0.02057168073952198, -0.007110764738172293, -0.025261957198381424, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.2040065485052764e-05, -0.054958246648311615, -0.03815570846199989, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0003357561945449561, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, -0.0053568